WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.487
An algorithm is steps in
words. A computer needs code.

2
00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:12.050
Blocks are code. Blocks
in a row are a program.

3
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:18.773
An algorithm is a set of steps in
words. Move right. Jump. Say hello.

4
00:00:18.993 --> 00:00:23.916
A computer cannot read our sentences.
It needs the steps as code.

5
00:00:24.136 --> 00:00:27.898
Code is instructions in a
form the computer understands.

6
00:00:28.118 --> 00:00:32.901
So we use blocks. One block is
one instruction. Blocks are code.

7
00:00:33.121 --> 00:00:37.765
Blocks in a row are a program. A
program is code a computer runs.

8
00:00:38.265 --> 00:00:41.144
These are the seven blocks
the cat understands.

9
00:00:41.364 --> 00:00:45.822
Move right slides the cat one
space. Move left slides it back.

10
00:00:46.042 --> 00:00:49.618
Jump makes it hop. Say hello
gives it a speech bubble.

11
00:00:49.838 --> 00:00:54.436
Spin turns it round. Grow makes it
bigger and shrink makes it smaller.

12
00:00:54.656 --> 00:00:58.557
One block does one thing.
Two things need two blocks.

13
00:00:59.057 --> 00:01:02.215
To build a program, read
the algorithm first.

14
00:01:02.435 --> 00:01:06.568
It says move right, then jump.
Two steps, so two blocks.

15
00:01:06.788 --> 00:01:10.178
Pick the move right block
first. That is step one.

16
00:01:10.398 --> 00:01:12.999
Then pick the jump
block. That is step two.

17
00:01:13.219 --> 00:01:18.234
The computer does the blocks in the order
you place them. Match the algorithm.

18
00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:22.310
Here is a program you did not
build. What will the cat do?

19
00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:26.710
Read every block, left to right.
Do not read just the first one.

20
00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:30.087
Move right. Move right again. Then jump.

21
00:01:30.307 --> 00:01:35.973
Saying what will happen before it runs is
predicting. Programmers do it all the time.

22
00:01:36.473 --> 00:01:39.817
Now press Run. The computer
does the blocks in order.

23
00:01:40.037 --> 00:01:43.380
Watch the cat. Did it do
what the algorithm said?

24
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.619
Running a program to check
it is called testing.

25
00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:50.461
If it did the wrong thing, change
the blocks and run it again.

26
00:01:50.681 --> 00:01:55.465
A computer cannot think for
itself. It does what it is told.

27
00:01:55.965 --> 00:02:00.005
A program does not only run on
a tablet. Look around your home.

28
00:02:00.225 --> 00:02:03.569
Many everyday things have
a small computer inside.

29
00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:08.433
A traffic light runs a program:
red, then amber, then green.

30
00:02:08.653 --> 00:02:12.693
A washing machine runs one
too: fill, wash, spin, drain.

31
00:02:12.913 --> 00:02:16.907
A robot vacuum runs a program.
A game is a program too.

32
00:02:17.407 --> 00:02:22.794
An algorithm in words becomes code.
Code a computer runs is a program.

33
00:02:23.014 --> 00:02:26.079
Build it, predict it,
then run it to test it.

34
00:02:26.299 --> 00:02:30.432
A computer does what your program
says. Programs are everywhere.
